-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  exe_cli_errors_value.pcpp - Build-kind compliance: an option without its
  value

  An option that takes a value, given none (-o needs a path): exit 2. An
  error about one argument's value says what is wrong with it, so it gives
  no hint to run pcpp -h (a usage error does). This file itself is never
  compiled.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe exe_cli_errors_value;

/*
  @@test
    kind cli
    args "--no-banner <DIR>/fixtures/exe_cli_hello.pcpp -o"
    exitcode 2
    expect
    | Error: -o requires a path argument
  @@end
*/

begin
end.
